{"id": "EUVD-2026-77372", "enisaUuid": "50556a79-16f5-3c73-a3e5-e8d478a04406", "description": "Insertion of sensitive information into log file vulnerability in Apache Syncope.\n\n\n\nWhen AES key of non-standard length (not 16/24/32 bytes) is configured, Syncope will pad the provided value with random characters. The resulting key value is logged.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Syncope: from 3.0.15 through 3.0.16, from 4.0.3 through 4.0.7, from 4.1.0-M0 through 4.1.2.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 4.0.8 / 4.1.3, which fix this issue.", "datePublished": "2026-09-14T10:42:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-14T19:46:26", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://lists.apache.org/thread/3t3om8mny7ng52q053pdzpmtdtosnqoo"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-87779", "GHSA-2987-fvqf-8g2j"], "assigner": "apache", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b4e1f0f9-bec4-34df-880e-90ff8c3d9a73", "product": {"name": "Apache Syncope", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "4.1.0-M0 \u22644.1.2"}, {"id": "d69c9c71-8b28-34c7-8b88-23dc33b2f8f9", "product": {"name": "Apache Syncope", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "3.0.15 \u22643.0.16"}, {"id": "f4048fa1-7c23-35e1-8a5c-2df567ee80bc", "product": {"name": "Apache Syncope", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "4.0.3 \u22644.0.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0843a2da-dc4b-3b59-a9d1-d0e5e8d0e81e", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}